{"name":"Light Raw Cotton","hex":"#ecdfca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"raw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Rawang."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not cooked. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Subsisting on, or pertaining to, a diet of raw food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raw"},{"term":"cotton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous substance:\n A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium.\n Any similar soft, fibrous, white substance of fine hairs, of any origin.","A soft, fibrous, usually white substance consisting of fine hairs, especially the substance around the seeds of a plant of genus Gossypium."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of cotton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cotton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPlant.JPG/330px-CottonPlant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton","wikidata":"Q11457"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg/500px-BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg/1280px-BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg/500px-BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cotton ready for harvest in Andhra Pradesh, India.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABALLS_OF_COTTON_(ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA)_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Mehrgarh_pakistan_rel96.JPG/500px-Mehrgarh_pakistan_rel96.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia